window.docContents[130].resolve({"/part-1-foundations/ch05-shadows-and-primes/#ch05-shadows-and-primes":{"contents":"Chapter 5 harvests the geometric payoff of Part I inside Ch05_HyperrealsGreatAndSmall.lean:\n\n* Halos & Galaxies: Two hyperreals lie in the same halo (x \\approx_h y) when x - y \\in \\mathbb{I} is infinitesimal, and in the same galaxy when x - y \\in \\mathbb{L} is limited.* The Standard Part (shadow): For every limited b \\in \\mathbb{L}, the cut \\{r \\in \\mathbb{R} : (r : \\mathbb{R}^*) < b\\} is nonempty and bounded above in \\mathbb{R}. By Dedekind completeness of \\mathbb{R}, its supremum \\mathrm{sh}(b) \\in \\mathbb{R} exists and is the unique real number infinitesimally close to b!* Valuation Ring Isomorphism: Limited hyperreals form a subring \\mathbb{L} \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}^*, infinitesimals form a maximal ideal \\mathbb{I} \\triangleleft \\mathbb{L}, and shadowRingHom induces a canonical ring isomorphism \\mathbb{L} / \\mathbb{I} \\simeq_{+\\,*} \\mathbb{R}!* Euclid's Infinitude of Primes via Hypernaturals: Pick an unlimited hypernatural N \\in \\mathbb{N}^* \\setminus \\mathbb{N}. By Transfer of prime factorization, N! + 1 has a hyperprime divisor P \\in {}^*\\mathrm{Prime}. Since P divides N! + 1, P cannot divide N!, so P > n for every standard n \\in \\mathbb{N}. By backward existential transfer, the set of standard primes is unbounded!\n\nsection\nopen Goldblatt\n\n-- Every limited hyperreal is infinitesimally close to its unique real shadow:\n#check @infClose_shadow\n#check @shadow_add\n#check @shadow_mul\n#check @ker_shadowRingHom\n\n-- Euclid's theorem proved via a hyperprime dividing N! + 1 for unlimited N:\n#check nonstandard_euclid_infinite_primes\nend\n\n\n","context":"Lectures on the Hyperreals — Interactive Lean 4 & Spatial Edition\u0009Part I — Foundations of the Hyperreal Line","header":"1.4. Chapter 5: Hyperreals Great & Small — Shadows, Quotients & Infinite Primes","id":"/part-1-foundations/ch05-shadows-and-primes/#ch05-shadows-and-primes"}});